construction risks. The results indicate that geological conditions and construction
management are the primary factors leading to accidents, providing targeted strategies for
construction risk management. A detailed safety construction risk analysis is proposed for
the shield tunneling phase of a specific metro project, along with corresponding
preventive measures and emergency plans, to reduce the probability of potential
construction risks and quickly mitigate their impact when accidents occur.
In summary, through in-depth safety construction risk analysis and scientific
preventive measures, this paper provides robust support for the safety construction of a
specific metro project. The research results not only hold significant reference value for
the safety management of metro engineering but also offer a universally applicable
research method and analysis framework for the safety construction risk management of
similar projects. Strengthening equipment quality supervision, operator training,
scientifically designing construction plans and geological predictions, and enhancing
construction management and monitoring control measures can effectively reduce
construction risks during shield tunnel construction, improving construction safety and
quality levels, and providing a feasible approach for the sustainable development of
engineering projects.
